WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.242
Selecting columns is one of the most common operations in Pandas.

00:00:04.242 --> 00:00:09.407
When we use one column name, Pandas usually returns a Series.

00:00:09.407 --> 00:00:16.347
When we provide several column names, Pandas returns a new DataFrame containing those columns.

00:00:16.347 --> 00:00:22.792
This matters because narrowing the table makes later analysis easier to read and reason about.

00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:31.167
If a dataset contains fifty columns but your question requires only customer I D, channel, and amount,

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:36.332
working with those relevant columns reduces visual and logical clutter.

00:00:36.332 --> 00:00:43.477
Run the example and compare the Python types of the one-column result and the two-column result.

00:00:43.477 --> 00:00:48.732
The values may look similar on screen, but they are different Pandas objects.
